{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/563787-changeling-mage-play-by-post-recruiting","id":563787,"title":"Changeling/Mage play-by-post recruiting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-22T00:21:24-07:00","id":563787,"title":"Changeling/Mage play-by-post recruiting","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I'm running a Changeling play-by-post game over at RPoL and we're currently open to new members. I've also opened the game to Mage players, as I'll shortly be introducing some opportunities for characters from the Traditions to join in.<br /> <br /> The game is here: <a href=\"http://www.rpol.net/gameinfo.php?gi=63447&amp;date=1434957197\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.rpol.net/gameinfo.php?gi=...ate=1434957197</a><br /> <br /> The themes are magic and technology. It's my idea that the game will segue into Changeling 20 when that comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T01:18:48-07:00","id":563807,"title":"","content":"sounds fun. I've never played a play by post game sadly so I'm a little fuzzy on the details on when and how though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5767,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","user":"DeeDee","date":".  So I just read the character creation guidelines and I have a couple of questions. I'm thinking a verbena mage with the fae blood merit. I have little to no expirence with kinian and was wondering h 06-22-2015, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T10:20:51-07:00","id":564237,"title":"","content":"Hey DeeDee, <br /> <br /> It's really simple. If you check out the boards, you'll see how it's done in practice. The older scenes are summaries of play by live chat (we stopped that after everyone's schedules get hectic). The latest scene has examples of play and dice rolls, which makes it easier to grasp.<br /> <br /> In short: I open each scene with a bit of description. Each player announces their character in the scene and states any objectives they have in brackets at the end.<br /> <br /> Players then take it in turns interacting freely with each other, while I narrate the actions of any NPCs and add in any changes in circumstances that may occur. <br /> <br /> If a player wants to make a roll, I tell them which stats and which difficulty they need to roll, and they use the Dice Roller app in the game for resolution. If I call for a roll, I tell everyone what to roll, and they do so as soon as they're next able. Then I summarise the outcome of the dice rolls before we move onto the next action.<br /> <br /> In general, it's pretty easy to pick up. The pace is dictated by players, and most interactions don't require dice rolls unless there's an important slot development at stake. People fall into an easy turn-taking rhythm, so that everyone gets a chance to act and react.<br /> <br /> If you're still interested, request to join the game on RPoL and we can chat further :-)","signa